# The free online answer in the chat (D-191): when the documents hold no answer, a free online model answers and the
# local Guardian checks it against the pages it names and Wikipedia articles it finds itself. No Claude, nothing paid.
# Without any key here it uses Pollinations, which needs none (one answer every 45 seconds). With a key, Groq or
# OpenRouter answers instead, faster and with more models. Copy this file to free.local.env (git and Docker ignore
# that name) and fill in the keys you have; or set the same names as environment variables. Never commit a key.

# https://console.groq.com/keys (free tier)
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_your-key
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# https://openrouter.ai/keys (free models end in :free; 50 requests a day)
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-your-key
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free

# Use one service only: groq, openrouter or pollinations. Empty: the first whose key is set, else pollinations.
# TG_FREE_PROVIDER=
